{"id":"36fb01abd4e8dac1","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-df-boundary-operator.md","title":"Boundary Operator","display":"df-boundary-operator — Boundary Operator","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-boundary-operator","aliases":["58-df-boundary-operator","Boundary Operator"],"display":"df-boundary-operator — Boundary Operator","depends_on":["[[58-df-chain-complex]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-boundary-operator"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-boundary-operator</span><span>Boundary Operator</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-boundary-operator — Boundary Operator"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"c3537edf2017d84e\" href=\"?note=c3537edf2017d84e\" title=\"58-df-chain-complex\">58-df-chain-complex</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C,+,\\partial\\in V\">\\(C,+,\\partial\\in V\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d\\in V\">\\(d\\in V\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\mathbb Z\">\\(n\\in\\mathbb Z\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ChainComplex}_S(C,+,\\partial)\">\\(\\mathrm{ChainComplex}_S(C,+,\\partial)\\)</span> (chain-complex predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"c3537edf2017d84e\" href=\"?note=c3537edf2017d84e\" title=\"58-df-chain-complex\">58-df-chain-complex</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BoundaryOperator}_S(d,n;C,+,\\partial)\">\\(\\mathrm{BoundaryOperator}_S(d,n;C,+,\\partial)\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}boundary\\text{-}operator} \\vdash \\mathrm{BoundaryOperator}_S(d,n;C,+,\\partial)\\leftrightarrow d\\in V\\land\\mathrm{ChainComplex}_S(C,+,\\partial)\\land n\\in\\mathbb Z\\land d=\\partial(n)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}boundary\\text{-}operator} \\vdash \\mathrm{BoundaryOperator}_S(d,n;C,+,\\partial)\\leftrightarrow d\\in V\\land\\mathrm{ChainComplex}_S(C,+,\\partial)\\land n\\in\\mathbb Z\\land d=\\partial(n)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Boundary operator: maps <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span>-chains to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(n-1)\">\\((n-1)\\)</span>-chains</li>\n<li>For a simplicial chain complex the usual alternating face formula is the construction of the family <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\partial\">\\(\\partial\\)</span>; it is not asserted here without a separately defined oriented-chain basis.</li>\n<li>Chain complex: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\cdots \\to C_n \\xrightarrow{\\partial_n} C_{n-1} \\to \\cdots\">\\(\\cdots \\to C_n \\xrightarrow{\\partial_n} C_{n-1} \\to \\cdots\\)</span></li>\n<li>Homology: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H_n = \\ker \\partial_n / \\mathrm{im} \\partial_{n+1}\">\\(H_n = \\ker \\partial_n / \\mathrm{im} \\partial_{n+1}\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Hatcher, Algebraic Topology</li>\n<li>Munkres, Elements of Algebraic Topology</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-chain-complex","status":"resolved","id":"c3537edf2017d84e","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-chain-complex]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-chain-complex","status":"resolved","id":"c3537edf2017d84e","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{ChainComplex}_S(C,+,\\partial)$ (chain-complex predicate, see [[58-df-chain-complex]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"C,+,\\partial\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"d\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"n\\in\\mathbb Z","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ChainComplex}_S(C,+,\\partial)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{BoundaryOperator}_S(d,n;C,+,\\partial)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}boundary\\text{-}operator} \\vdash \\mathrm{BoundaryOperator}_S(d,n;C,+,\\partial)\\leftrightarrow d\\in V\\land\\mathrm{ChainComplex}_S(C,+,\\partial)\\land n\\in\\mathbb Z\\land d=\\partial(n)","display":true},{"tex":"n","display":false},{"tex":"(n-1)","display":false},{"tex":"\\partial","display":false},{"tex":"\\cdots \\to C_n \\xrightarrow{\\partial_n} C_{n-1} \\to \\cdots","display":false},{"tex":"H_n = \\ker \\partial_n / \\mathrm{im} \\partial_{n+1}","display":false}],"bytes":1248,"backlinks":[{"id":"a11585cba9c21cfd","anchor":"ref-242","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[58-df-boundary-operator]]"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-204","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-df-boundary-operator.md|58-df-boundary-operator]]（batch20）"}],"outgoing":["c3537edf2017d84e"]}